From 494bae7e23f06da0fbe9ca206d2f765e1213f093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blame42 <346530647+git-blame-42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:41:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Validate that the event creator exists and is an admin

Add a generic Validations::exists that checks the attribute is the id of a record of the given model, with optional extra conditions. Event::validates uses it for user_id and then requires the creator to be an admin, so an unknown user_id is a validation error instead of a foreign key PDOException. Since user_id is not a form field, the form shows its error in an alert above the fields.
---
